    "issues": [],
    "pullRequests": [
      {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/Squirrel.Windows/pulls/2",
        "id": 709599200,
        "node_id": "MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NzA5NTk5MjAw",
        "number": 2,
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "Make directory deletion more atomic",
        "user": {
          "login": "mikepavone",
          "id": 157731,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzczMQ==",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/mikepavone",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "Currently, if a file is locked in the destination directory (which will be the case if the app is running), it will end up partially deleted and the installation will exit with an error. This leaves the existing install in a corrupted state, which is less than ideal. This PR makes deletes sort-of atomic by first renaming the directory before deleting it. This rename will fail if the app is currently running or if the contents of the directory happen to be locked for some other reason",
        "created_at": "2021-08-11T20:41:17Z",
        "updated_at": "2021-09-14T00:12:26Z",
        "closed_at": "2021-09-14T00:12:12Z",
        "merged_at": "2021-09-14T00:12:12Z",
