      {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/Squirrel.Windows/pulls/1",
        "id": 35190840,
        "node_id": "MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MzUxOTA4NDA=",
        "number": 1,
        "state": "closed",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "Feature/fixsetup",
        "user": {
          "login": "jasoncitron",
          "id": 90868,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjkwODY4",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jasoncitron",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "Fixes a few high priority UX bugs in the installer.\n- Uninstall now attempts to delete its folder 10 times (with a 1 second sleep between each). This fixes our \"not everything is uninstalled upon uninstall\" issue. Update.exe unfortunately remains.\n- Updating now waits 10 seconds instead of 2 seconds to acquire the global squirrel lock. This fixes the issue where upon the first launch updating would immediately fail, because the installer was still running and had the squirrel lock.\n- Checking no longer attempts to return release notes, since they are guaranteed to not be present. ReleaseNotes come from the nuget, which we are not downloading in Check.\n- Just some extra logging too.\n",
        "created_at": "2015-05-12T03:41:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2015-05-12T18:31:33Z",
